        "original_id": "c71b21a1-c1ce-540c-a4a1-ce6d78a0b5c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Wadleigh, Barbara Kopple, Cathy Caplan, Thomas Haneke, Lawrence Silk\n- Films: Woodstock, American Dream, Harlan County, U.S.A.\n- Events: Woodstock Festival, Hormel Foods strike\n- Places: Bethel, New York, Austin, Minnesota, Akron, Ohio\n\nFacts:\n- The Woodstock Festival took place in August 1969 near Bethel, New York.\n- Michael Wadleigh was born on September 24, 1942, in Akron, Ohio.\n- Michael Wadleigh is an American film director and cinematographer known for the documentary film \"Woodstock\" about the 1969 Woodstock Festival.\n- \"Woodstock\" is a 1970 documentary film about the counterculture Woodstock Festival.\n- Barbara Kopple directed and produced \"Harlan County, U.S.A.\" and has long advocated for workers' rights.\n- \"American Dream\" is a 1990 cinéma vérité documentary film directed by Barbara Kopple and co-directed by Cathy Caplan, Thomas Haneke, and Lawrence Silk.\n- \"American Dream\" recounts the Hormel Foods strike in Austin, Minnesota, in 1985–86.\n- \"Harlan County, U.S.A.\" is less ambivalent toward unions than Barbara Kopple's later film \"American Dream.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
